<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  notificationTimeout MUST stay 0. Any non-zero value makes the platform
  coalesce same-type events, which collapses a scroll burst into one callback
  and destroys stall responsiveness.

  canRetrieveWindowContent MUST stay false. We only read event.packageName,
  which arrives on the event object itself. Requesting content reads is a
  privacy and performance cost with no benefit here, and it is the single flag
  Play reviewers scrutinise hardest.

  isAccessibilityTool MUST stay false. This is a friction tool, not an
  assistive one; claiming otherwise is a Play Console policy violation.

  packageNames scopes the event firehose. It is re-set at runtime via
  setServiceInfo() when the user edits their target list, see
  MolassesAccessibilityService.applyTargets().

  dev.molasses is in the list on purpose. Without it no event arrives when the
  user leaves a target app, so the session is never closed and time keeps
  accruing against an app that is no longer on screen. Including it means every
  overlay this app shows now produces events too, which is why
  ForegroundEventRouter drops anything wearing our own package name before it
  looks at anything else.

  packageNames MUST stay scoped to the monitored targets plus dev.molasses.
  Banking and UPI apps read the declared AccessibilityServiceInfo of every
  enabled service, and a service scoped to all packages is what trips their
  "Suspicious App Detected" warning hardest. Widening this list is a user-
  visible regression on a daily-driver phone, not a refactor.

  flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows was REMOVED for the same reason. It is one of
  the flags those apps inspect, and it is the one that reads as "this service
  can enumerate and inspect every window on screen". We do not need it:
  getWindows() was only ever used for the overlay collision guard and for Bit's
  fullscreen auto-retract, and both have replacements that need no flag. See
  MolassesAccessibilityService.ownWindowIds and the README section on
  banking-app compatibility.

  Removing it is not free. getWindows() now returns an empty list, so anything
  that wants to know about other windows has to go through UsageStatsManager
  instead. Do not add the flag back to make a window query work; find another
  route or drop the feature.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeViewScrolled|typeWindowStateChanged|typeWindowsChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagDefault"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="false"
    android:canPerformGestures="false"
    android:notificationTimeout="0"
    android:packageNames="dev.molasses,com.instagram.android,com.twitter.android,com.google.android.youtube"
    android:isAccessibilityTool="false"
    android:settingsActivity="dev.molasses.ui.settings.SettingsActivity"
    android:description="@string/a11y_service_description"/>
